# Android services stubbed out on the Minimal Phone MP01 under LuneOS/Halium
# (see meta-android's pre-start.d/50-stub-services; picked by the vendor
# codename "MP01").
#
# Fingerprint HALs. Both block forever inside the TrustKernel TEE driver
# (tee_supp_cmd -> down) waiting for the TEE supplicant, which never answers
# under LuneOS. A thread parked there is uninterruptible and refuses to
# freeze, so every suspend attempt aborted with "One or more tasks refusing
# to freeze" - measured 2026-09-19: 3240 aborts in 90 minutes, not one
# suspend, until the phone was rebooted with these stubbed. Fingerprint stays
# unavailable on this device until the TEE supplicant works; nothing else in
# the container uses the TEE at runtime.
vendor/bin/hw/android.hardware.biometrics.fingerprint@2.1-service
vendor/bin/hw/vendor.focaltech.hardware.biometrics.fingerprint@1.0-service
# Android's USB-OTG storage FUSE daemon (service fuse_usbotg in
# init.project.rc runs /system/bin/sdcard for /storage/usbotg). Nothing mounts
# OTG media into the container under LuneOS, so it exits at once and init
# restarts it every five seconds for the life of the boot - 12 starts a minute,
# each with a flags_health_check exec, a third of the kernel log line rate
# measured on the MP01. No other service in this image uses sdcard.
system/bin/sdcard
# The combo-chip firmware dump collector (service stp_dump in
# init.connectivity.rc runs /vendor/bin/stp_dump3). With no Android framework
# to hand a dump to, it busy-loops: measured on the MP01, 93 % of a CPU core
# continuously and 121 minutes of CPU time in a 4h23m uptime, which is the
# single largest awake-time drain on the device. It collects diagnostics only;
# nothing in LuneOS consumes them. Same treatment as tissot's wcnss_filter.
vendor/bin/stp_dump3
